is about ±10%, but this variation is masked by the uncertainty of quantifying the surface roughness.” One of the (rare explicit) comments on Colebrook’s equation (12) is given in [13] in which White comments that ”the equation (12) is accurate to ±15% percent for design calculations over the full range of Re and Rr. It can be used for circular and noncircular
